/-!
# The deltoidal hexecontahedron as a fivefold solid model

The deltoidal hexecontahedron, in a frame where z is a 5-fold axis: 70
vertex slots, 14 seed vertices rotated about z in steps of 2π/5 (slot
`14k + s` is seed `s` rotated by `2πk/5`, up to rounding). The two vertices
on the z axis fill five slots each, so the 70 slots hold the solid's 62
vertices. `slotVertices` is the certified rational model (dyadic
coordinates), generated by the C++ search from the model file and copied
here by the branch's `scripts/update_vertices.py`. Vertices are scaled to lie
inside the unit sphere (the GoodPoly invariant).

`icosahedralSolid` (a scoped instance: in effect inside `namespace
DeltoidalHexecontahedron` only) makes this data, with its I-orbit tables
(`OrbitData`), an `IcosahedralSolid`, hence a `FivefoldSolid` and a
`SolidModel` for the certificate pipeline; the facts it needs are checked by
the kernel below.
-/

namespace DeltoidalHexecontahedron

open Noperts Noperts.Pipeline

